Each check day: set-up and settling 3 minutes, the written sitting (or the short making task with its written items)
32, collecting work 3, clean-up 2, inside the 40 minutes; a student may answer a written item aloud at the teacher's
table. Every student's evidence is collected once in a window; no artifact is scored twice. Days above are band
course days (year 7 starts on day 65, year 8 on day 129).

## Cross-subject

Four visual arts rows of grades 6 to 8 carry a cross_subject lean (data/progressions/arts.csv); each is a same-year
lean on a core course, each core frame is written, and each teaches its part before this course's unit uses it
(art course days map to school days as in the Days bullet: year days 35 to 48 fall on school days 88 to 120, year
days 49 to 62 on school days 123 to 155, year days 35 to 50 on school days 88 to 125). All leans are on core courses
(lesson 32).

