{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '7', 'skill_id': 'va-g7-ideas', 'standard': 'VA:Cr1.1.7a; VA:Cr1.2.7a', 'assumes': 'va-g6-ideas', 'hands_on': 'va-g8-ideas', 'model_in': 'sketchbook', 'model_out': 'sketchbook', 'words': 'stuck; strategy; guideline; aim; limit; restart', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Use strategies to get past being stuck (change the material, set a limit, start from a different edge), and write guidelines to steer a work toward a stated aim. What changes: strategies for being stuck and written guidelines. Assessed by a planning page and a short talk, scored on a rubric for range of ideas and use of research.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'va-g8-ideas', 'standard': 'VA:Cr1.1.8a; VA:Cr1.2.8a', 'assumes': 'va-g7-ideas', 'hands_on': 'va-g9-ideas', 'model_in': 'sketchbook', 'model_out': 'sketchbook', 'words': 'record; process; inquiry; contemporary; daily life; medium', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Keep a record of early creative steps as pictures or words in an old or new medium, and with a group shape a question about modern daily life that draws on current art or design. What changes: the record of early steps is kept as it happens, and the group inquiry looks at the present day, not a past style. Assessed by a planning page and a short talk, scored on a rubric for range of ideas and use of research.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'va-g9-ideas', 'standard': 'VA:Cr1.1.Ia; VA:Cr1.2.Ia', 'assumes': 'va-g8-ideas', 'hands_on': 'va-g10-ideas', 'model_in': 'sketchbook', 'model_out': 'sketchbook', 'words': 'route; start; inquiry; contemporary; practice; design', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Start one project three ways (a word web, a thumbnail page, a photo walk), pick the strongest, and frame a question about daily life today that a current artist or designer has also taken up. What changes: the student tries several start routes and frames a question about daily life through current practice, with no teacher-set prompt as in grade 8. Assessed by a planning portfolio entry scored on a rubric for range, research and a stated aim. Level 1 bridge: the first unit teaches the grade 8 techniques and words Level 1 needs, as readiness, and claims no grade 8 id (at most 12 days in the full year, 6 on the 80-day short path, STANDARD.md 3.2).'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'va-g5-craft', 'standard': 'VA:Cr2.1.5a; VA:Cr2.2.5a', 'assumes': 'va-g4-craft', 'hands_on': 'va-g6-craft', 'model_in': 'safe-studio; practice-log', 'model_out': 'safe-studio; practice-log', 'words': 'practice; skill; craft; care; log; technique', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Build skill in several techniques through experiments and practice logged in the sketchbook, and show fine craft by caring for and using supplies and tools well. What changes: practice is logged and craft means care. Assessed by a studio task scored on a short rubric for safe handling, care of materials and trying a new technique.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '6', 'skill_id': 'va-g6-craft', 'standard': 'VA:Cr2.1.6a; VA:Cr2.2.6a', 'assumes': 'va-g5-craft', 'hands_on': 'va-g7-craft', 'model_in': 'safe-studio; practice-log', 'model_out': 'safe-studio; practice-log', 'words': 'open; new method; environment; waste; reuse; cleanup', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Show openness to new ideas, materials and methods, and explain how saving, caring for and cleaning up supplies affects the environment (waste, rinse water, reuse). What changes: the student explains the environmental cost of waste and rinse water, where grade 5 judged craft by care alone. Assessed by a studio task and a practice log, scored on a rubric for safe handling, skill growth and persistence.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '7', 'skill_id': 'va-g7-craft', 'standard': 'VA:Cr2.1.7a; VA:Cr2.2.7a', 'assumes': 'va-g6-craft', 'hands_on': 'va-g8-craft', 'model_in': 'safe-studio; practice-log', 'model_out': 'safe-studio; practice-log', 'words': 'persist; skill; online; permission; share; duty', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Work one piece through several sessions in two or more media, keeping a process log of what was tried and fixed, and plan how a photo of it would be shared online with permission and no faces or names. What changes: persistence is shown over weeks and sharing carries duty. Assessed by a studio task and a practice log, scored on a rubric for safe handling, skill growth and persistence.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'va-g8-craft', 'standard': 'VA:Cr2.1.8a; VA:Cr2.2.8a', 'assumes': 'va-g7-craft', 'hands_on': 'va-g9-craft', 'model_in': 'safe-studio; practice-log', 'model_out': 'safe-studio; practice-log', 'words': 'risk; invent; copyright; fair use; open license; borrow', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Take a planned risk in one piece (a new medium, scale or subject) and log what it meant to the work, then label each borrowed image in the piece as own, open license or public domain, with credit. What changes: the student takes a risk with an idea and explains how copyright and open licenses apply to own work, where grade 7 attended to sharing images. Assessed by a studio task and a practice log, scored on a rubric for safe handling, skill growth and persistence. Teacher note: only public domain or openly licensed sources are used as models in the unit.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'va-g9-craft', 'standard': 'VA:Cr2.1.Ia; VA:Cr2.2.Ia', 'assumes': 'va-g8-craft', 'hands_on': 'va-g10-craft', 'model_in': 'safe-studio; practice-log', 'model_out': 'safe-studio; practice-log', 'words': 'unplanned; material; hazard; health; ventilation; safety', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Make an artwork or design without planning it first, to learn what the materials do, and explain how materials can affect people's health and nature while handling them safely. What changes: the student makes without planning first to learn what a material does, and explains its health and nature effects, with the hazard sheet read before use. Assessed by a studio task and a portfolio entry, scored on a rubric for safe handling, skill growth and sound reasons. Teacher note: a hazard sheet for each material is read before use; ventilation and cleanup are shown."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'va-g5-design', 'standard': 'VA:Cr2.3.5a; VA:Cn10.1.5a', 'assumes': 'va-g4-design', 'hands_on': 'va-g6-design', 'model_in': 'design-brief', 'model_out': 'design-brief', 'words': 'place; object; matters; record; vocabulary; symmetry', 'cross_subject': 'math:4.G.A.3 (finding lines of symmetry in a design)', 'notes': 'Draw a map or a set of sketches of places and objects that matter to the student, labeled with art and design words, and use the labels to point out one thing never noticed before. What changes: choosing what matters and using the vocabulary. Assessed by a made product scored on a short rubric for a clear purpose, use of the given need and care in making.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '6', 'skill_id': 'va-g6-design', 'standard': 'VA:Cr2.3.6a; VA:Cn10.1.6a', 'assumes': 'va-g5-design', 'hands_on': 'va-g7-design', 'model_in': 'design-brief', 'model_out': 'design-brief', 'words': 'user; need; rework; system; design; interest', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Create or rework an object, place or system for the stated needs of named users, and note what each user needs, starting from a collection of ideas drawn from current interests and concerns, with a public or invented option marked the same. What changes: a design is made for named users and their stated needs, not for the maker's taste. Assessed by a made product and a design note, scored on a rubric for meeting the stated need and clear organizing."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '7', 'skill_id': 'va-g7-design', 'standard': 'VA:Cr2.3.7a; VA:Cn10.1.7a', 'assumes': 'va-g6-design', 'hands_on': 'va-g8-design', 'model_in': 'design-brief', 'model_out': 'design-brief', 'words': 'hierarchy; layout; contrast; scale; information; gather', 'cross_subject': 'math:7.G.A.1 (a scale drawing of a layout)', 'notes': 'Apply visual organizing strategies (hierarchy, grouping, scale, contrast) to make work that clearly shares information, and make a visual record (a map, sketches or photos with no faces) of where and when people gather for art in the community. What changes: a design job is now organizing information so a viewer reads it clearly, where grade 6 met the needs of users. Assessed by a made product and a design note, scored on a rubric for meeting the stated need and clear organizing.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'va-g8-design', 'standard': 'VA:Cr2.3.8a; VA:Cn10.1.8a', 'assumes': 'va-g7-design', 'hands_on': 'va-g9-design', 'model_in': 'design-brief', 'model_out': 'design-brief', 'words': 'layout; text; image; presentation; group identity; audience', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Pick and arrange pictures and text so a presentation is clear and compelling to an audience, and make art with a group that reflects on and strengthens the good side of a group's identity (the class, the school, a team or an invented group). What changes: pictures and text are arranged together for an audience, where grade 7 organized information alone. Assessed by a made product and a design note, scored on a rubric for meeting the stated need and clear organizing."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'va-g9-design', 'standard': 'VA:Cr2.3.Ia; VA:Cn10.1.Ia', 'assumes': 'va-g8-design', 'hands_on': 'va-g10-design', 'model_in': 'design-brief', 'model_out': 'design-brief', 'words': 'propose; space; experience; develop; spark; model', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'With a small team, sketch and model a change to one school space that would alter how people move or feel there, and keep an idea log from first sketch to final proposal. What changes: the student proposes a change to one place with others, drawn and modeled, and records how an idea grew, where grade 8 made art together without a site. Assessed by a made product and a written rationale, scored on a rubric for the stated need, the audience and the use of art vocabulary. Teacher note: proposals are drawings and models; nothing is built on school grounds without permission.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'va-g5-revise', 'standard': 'VA:Cr3.1.5a', 'assumes': 'va-g4-revise', 'hands_on': 'va-g6-revise', 'model_in': 'talk-about-choices; critique-protocol', 'model_out': 'talk-about-choices; critique-protocol; artist-statement', 'words': 'artist statement; explain; choice; revise; art words; critique', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Write an artist statement that uses art words to explain choices, then revise the work and the statement after a critique. What changes: the child writes an artist statement, where grade 4 spoke in a critique. Assessed by a critique and a revised piece, scored on a short rubric for using classmate talk and art words.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '6', 'skill_id': 'va-g6-revise', 'standard': 'VA:Cr3.1.6a', 'assumes': 'va-g5-revise', 'hands_on': 'va-g7-revise', 'model_in': 'talk-about-choices; critique-protocol; artist-statement', 'model_out': 'talk-about-choices; critique-protocol; artist-statement', 'words': 'intent; viewer; match; revise; critique; message', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Check whether an artwork gets across what was meant, using a critique and a viewer's retelling, and change it to match. What changes: intent is compared with what viewers see. Assessed by a critique, a revised piece and a written statement, scored on a rubric for evidence and a reasoned change."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '7', 'skill_id': 'va-g7-revise', 'standard': 'VA:Cr3.1.7a', 'assumes': 'va-g6-revise', 'hands_on': 'va-g8-revise', 'model_in': 'talk-about-choices; critique-protocol; artist-statement', 'model_out': 'talk-about-choices; critique-protocol; artist-statement', 'words': 'reflect; key point; statement; format; explain; evidence', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Reflect on a work and explain its key points in a statement or another way (a recorded talk or a labeled sketch). What changes: the child picks the format of the reflection (a statement, a recorded talk or a labeled sketch). Assessed by a critique, a revised piece and a written statement, scored on a rubric for evidence and a reasoned change.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'va-g8-revise', 'standard': 'VA:Cr3.1.8a', 'assumes': 'va-g7-revise', 'hands_on': 'va-g9-revise', 'model_in': 'talk-about-choices; critique-protocol; artist-statement', 'model_out': 'talk-about-choices; critique-protocol; artist-statement', 'words': 'standard; examine; unfinished; plan; revise; criteria', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Use fitting standards to examine and think over unfinished art, then plan changes in writing before making them. What changes: named standards guide the examination of unfinished work and changes are planned in writing before they are made. Assessed by a critique, a revised piece and a written statement, scored on a rubric for evidence and a reasoned change. Teacher note: critique is of the work, never of the person.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'va-g9-revise', 'standard': 'VA:Cr3.1.Ia', 'assumes': 'va-g8-revise', 'hands_on': 'va-g10-revise', 'model_in': 'talk-about-choices; critique-protocol; artist-statement', 'model_out': 'talk-about-choices; critique-protocol; artist-statement', 'words': 'standard; culture; review; revise; unfinished; past', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Use standards from past and present cultures to review and revise unfinished art, naming whose standards are used. What changes: the review uses standards from more than one culture and names whose they are. Assessed by a critique, a revised piece and an artist statement, scored on a rubric for standards used, reasons given and the quality of the revision.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'va-g5-show', 'standard': 'VA:Pr4.1.5a; VA:Pr5.1.5a', 'assumes': 'va-g4-show', 'hands_on': 'va-g6-show', 'model_in': 'exhibit-plan', 'model_out': 'exhibit-plan', 'words': 'curator; care; role; safe; prepare; argue', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Take the curator's job for a small class show: list the care and display jobs, then argue for one set of safe materials and one way of mounting the work, with reasons. What changes: a named role and an argument with reasons. Assessed by a display task and a short written note, scored on a rubric for a clear plan and a reason for each choice."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '6', 'skill_id': 'va-g6-show', 'standard': 'VA:Pr4.1.6a; VA:Pr5.1.6a', 'assumes': 'va-g5-show', 'hands_on': 'va-g7-show', 'model_in': 'exhibit-plan', 'model_out': 'exhibit-plan', 'words': 'flat; 3D; digital; display plan; viewer; layout', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Compare how flat, three-dimensional and digital art are kept and shown, and draw a display plan, alone or in a group, that fits space, viewers and layout. What changes: a drawn display plan replaces a talk about spaces. Assessed by a display plan and a spoken talk, scored on a rubric for audience, space and reasons.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '7', 'skill_id': 'va-g7-show', 'standard': 'VA:Pr4.1.7a; VA:Pr5.1.7a', 'assumes': 'va-g6-show', 'hands_on': 'va-g8-show', 'model_in': 'exhibit-plan', 'model_out': 'exhibit-plan', 'words': 'compare; technology; standard; judge; method; viewing', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Compare how a work is kept and seen in a gallery, in print and on a screen, then score two ways of preparing the class's work for showing against a set checklist. What changes: methods of preparing and showing are judged against standards, where grade 6 drew a plan. Assessed by a display plan and a spoken talk, scored on a rubric for audience, space and reasons."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'va-g8-show', 'standard': 'VA:Pr4.1.8a; VA:Pr5.1.8a', 'assumes': 'va-g7-show', 'hands_on': 'va-g9-show', 'model_in': 'exhibit-plan', 'model_out': 'exhibit-plan', 'words': 'standard; group show; theme; exhibition story; viewer; select', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Write the standards for picking a themed group of works, then with a team hang the show and write the wall stories viewers read. What changes: a group show goes up with written stories for its viewers, not a plan alone. Assessed by a display plan and a spoken talk, scored on a rubric for audience, space and reasons. Teacher note: a showing outside class needs each family's yes."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'va-g9-show', 'standard': 'VA:Pr4.1.Ia; VA:Pr5.1.Ia', 'assumes': 'va-g8-show', 'hands_on': 'va-g10-show', 'model_in': 'exhibit-plan', 'model_out': 'exhibit-plan', 'words': 'curate; analyze; exhibition; keep; choose; judge', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Choose and arrange works for a small show and for keeping, and write a short note on why a real exhibition is laid out the way it is. What changes: the student acts as curator and critic of a whole show, where grade 8 only planned one with a group. Assessed by an exhibition plan with written reasons, scored on a rubric for audience, space, care of the work and sound reasons.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'va-g5-museum', 'standard': 'VA:Pr6.1.5a; VA:Cn11.1.5a', 'assumes': 'va-g4-museum', 'hands_on': 'va-g6-museum', 'model_in': 'work-card', 'model_out': 'work-card', 'words': 'evidence; show; topic; belief; value; change', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Show from a real exhibit or its pages how it carries an idea or information on a topic, and describe how art can change what people believe, value or do. What changes: the student points to evidence in a real exhibit, not just describes what museums do. Assessed by a short written or spoken response citing one work and its setting, scored on a three-line guide. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '6', 'skill_id': 'va-g6-museum', 'standard': 'VA:Pr6.1.6a; VA:Cn11.1.6a', 'assumes': 'va-g5-museum', 'hands_on': 'va-g7-museum', 'model_in': 'work-card', 'model_out': 'work-card', 'words': 'community; history; value; mirror; custom; era', 'cross_subject': 'social-studies:ss6-paleolithic-neolithic (cave art studied with its time and place)', 'notes': "Study a local or online museum and judge, with evidence, how it shows its community's history and values, and trace how art changed with the era, the customs and the materials on hand. What changes: a museum is judged with evidence, where grade 5 pointed to evidence in one exhibit. Assessed by a source-based response that uses a work card for each work, scored on a rubric for evidence and a stated tie. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '7', 'skill_id': 'va-g7-museum', 'standard': 'VA:Pr6.1.7a; VA:Cn11.1.7a', 'assumes': 'va-g6-museum', 'hands_on': 'va-g8-museum', 'model_in': 'work-card', 'model_out': 'work-card', 'words': 'venue; collection; setting; supplies; reaction; compare', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Compare what it is like to view collections and exhibits in different venues, and analyze how knowing a work's era, place, supplies and uses shapes the way people react to it. What changes: the student compares what it is like to see an exhibit in different venues, and how knowing a work's era, place and use changes a reaction. Assessed by a source-based response that uses a work card for each work, scored on a rubric for evidence and a stated tie. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'va-g8-museum', 'standard': 'VA:Pr6.1.8a; VA:Cn11.1.8a', 'assumes': 'va-g7-museum', 'hands_on': 'va-g9-museum', 'model_in': 'work-card', 'model_out': 'work-card', 'words': 'influence; belief; collection; group identity; represent; mirror', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Study one exhibition or collection and explain how it shapes what visitors think and believe, then sort a set of works by how each shows, builds or reflects a group's identity. What changes: art is tied to group identity, where grade 7 compared venues. Assessed by a source-based response that uses a work card for each work, scored on a rubric for evidence and a stated tie. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'va-g9-museum', 'standard': 'VA:Pr6.1.Ia; VA:Cn11.1.Ia', 'assumes': 'va-g8-museum', 'hands_on': 'va-g10-museum', 'model_in': 'work-card', 'model_out': 'work-card', 'words': 'exhibit; society; politics; culture; custom; reaction', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Analyze how an exhibit shapes awareness of society, culture and politics, and describe how knowing a culture, its customs and history can change a viewer's reaction to a work. What changes: politics and society now enter the analysis of an exhibit, where grade 8 looked at group identity. Assessed by a source-based response with a work card for each work, scored on a rubric for evidence, setting and a reasoned claim. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'va-g5-look', 'standard': 'VA:Re7.1.5a; VA:Re7.2.5a', 'assumes': 'va-g4-look', 'hands_on': 'va-g6-look', 'model_in': 'look-describe-interpret', 'model_out': 'look-describe-interpret', 'words': 'reading; others; culture; link; image; compare', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Compare your own reading of an artwork with how others read it, and find and analyze cultural links a picture suggests. What changes: other readings are weighed, and culture becomes a clue in the picture. Assessed by a short spoken or written response using look-describe-interpret, scored on a three-line guide. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '6', 'skill_id': 'va-g6-look', 'standard': 'VA:Re7.1.6a; VA:Re7.2.6a', 'assumes': 'va-g5-look', 'hands_on': 'va-g7-look', 'model_in': 'look-describe-interpret', 'model_out': 'look-describe-interpret', 'words': 'interpret; persuade; culture; visual part; feeling; action', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Interpret art and design from more than one part of the world that shows how people live and what they value, and mark the visual parts and cultural ties that steer a viewer's ideas and feelings. What changes: the student analyzes how visual parts and cultural links sway ideas, feelings and actions, where grade 5 only found the links. Assessed by a written response using look-describe-interpret with evidence from the image, scored on a short rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '7', 'skill_id': 'va-g7-look', 'standard': 'VA:Re7.1.7a; VA:Re7.2.7a', 'assumes': 'va-g6-look', 'hands_on': 'va-g8-look', 'model_in': 'look-describe-interpret', 'model_out': 'look-describe-interpret', 'words': 'audience; display; location; value; sway; image', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Explain how the way a work is displayed, where it is and the viewer's own experience change how it is seen and valued, and analyze several ways images sway different audiences. What changes: display and audience join the picture as things that change meaning. Assessed by a written response using look-describe-interpret with evidence from the image, scored on a short rubric."}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'va-g8-look', 'standard': 'VA:Re7.1.8a; VA:Re7.2.8a', 'assumes': 'va-g7-look', 'hands_on': 'va-g9-look', 'model_in': 'look-describe-interpret', 'model_out': 'look-describe-interpret', 'words': 'taste; culture; setting; media; sway; image', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Explain from examples how culture and surroundings shape what people like and how they see themselves, and compare where viewers meet images that try to sway them (a billboard, a feed, a gallery). What changes: settings and media are compared, where grade 7 looked at audiences. Assessed by a written response using look-describe-interpret with evidence from the image, scored on a short rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'va', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'va-g9-look', 'standard': 'VA:Re7.1.Ia; VA:Re7.2.Ia', 'assumes': 'va-g8-look', 'hands_on': 'va-g10-look', 'model_in': 'look-describe-interpret', 'model_out': 'look-describe-interpret', 'words': 'perceive; experience; image; view; analyze; world', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Write a short proposal on how one set of artworks shapes how people understand a human experience, and reflect on how images seen every day shape the student's own view. What changes: the student looks at their own seeing, where grade 8 compared settings. Assessed by a written response with evidence from the image and its setting, scored on a rubric for evidence and reasoning."}
