188: ## Seams
189: 
190: ### Picked up from Visual Arts, grades 6 to 8
191: 
192: Visual Arts, grades 6 to 8 has no frame written, so this table is taken from the progression's grade 8 rows and the
193: Level 1 rows' `assumes` cells. Each grade 8 row is last used one grade back for a student who took that course
194: straight through; the bridge (unit 1) teaches its technique and words to every Level 1 student, and the paired unit
195: named below retrieves it on day 2.
196: 
197: | Grade 8 row hands on | What grade 8 did | Row that picks it up (Level 1, unit) | What Level 1 does with it |
198: |---|---|---|---|
199: | va-g8-ideas | A record of early steps; a group question about daily life | va-g9-ideas (unit 3) | Three start routes and a question of the student's own, with no teacher-set prompt |
200: | va-g8-craft | A planned risk; images labeled own, open license or public domain | va-g9-craft (unit 2) | Making without a plan; the health and nature effects of materials, with hazard cards |
201: | va-g8-design | Pictures and text arranged for an audience; group identity art | va-g9-design (unit 4) | A team proposal, drawn and modeled, for one school space, with an idea log |
202: | va-g8-revise | Named standards examine unfinished work; written change plans | va-g9-revise (unit 3) | Standards from past and present cultures, named as whose |
203: | va-g8-show | A themed group show with wall stories | va-g9-show (unit 5) | The student as curator of a small show and critic of a real exhibition's layout |
204: | va-g8-museum | An exhibition's sway on belief; works sorted by group identity | va-g9-museum (unit 5) | Society and politics in an exhibit's analysis; culture's effect on a viewer's reaction |
205: | va-g8-look | Taste and media settings compared | va-g9-look (unit 2) | A written proposal on how works shape understanding; the student's own seeing |
206: | va-g8-judge | A written analysis and an argued judgment | va-g9-judge (unit 4) | An interpretation with sufficient evidence; standards a jury would use |
207: 
208: ### Inside the band: level to level
209: 
210: Each row of Levels 2, 3 and 4 assumes the level before's row in its thread, taken the year before, so it opens as a
211: retrieval task inside day 2 of its unit.
212: 
213: | Thread | Level 1 row (unit, band days) | Level 2 row (unit) | Level 3 row (unit) | Level 4 row (unit) | What changes |
214: |---|---|---|---|---|---|
215: | Ideas | va-g9-ideas (unit 3, days 45 to 78) | va-g10-ideas (unit 8) | va-g11-ideas (unit 13) | va-g12-studio (unit 16) | Start routes, then problems from one's own work, then a plan for social change and a themed series, then a self-written proposal |
216: | Materials and ethics | va-g9-craft (unit 2, days 13 to 44) | va-g10-craft (unit 7) | va-g11-craft (unit 12) | va-g12-studio (unit 16); va-g12-purpose (unit 18) | Materials' health effects, then skill over a term and the ethics of sharing, then liberty against duty, then a record of ethical choices |
217: | Design and connecting | va-g9-design (unit 4, days 81 to 120) | va-g10-design (unit 9) | va-g11-design (unit 14) | va-g12-purpose (unit 18) | A proposal for one place, then a redesign for an issue, then a work on how images help or hinder lives, then a project for a real audience |
218: | Revision | va-g9-revise (unit 3, days 45 to 78) | va-g10-revise (unit 8) | va-g11-revise (unit 13) | va-g12-studio (unit 16) | Other cultures' standards, then one's own vision, then defended changes, then revision repeated on a self-led series |
219: | Showing | va-g9-show (unit 5, days 121 to 158) | va-g10-show (unit 10) | va-g11-show (unit 15) | va-g12-exhibit (unit 19) | A small show, then a sited portfolio show, then an event show with conservation, then a public exhibit |
220: | Museums and society | va-g9-museum (unit 5, days 121 to 158) | va-g10-museum (unit 10) | va-g11-museum (unit 15) | va-g12-exhibit (unit 19) | An exhibit's sway analyzed, then links argued, then a curated collection and a judged influence, then a public exhibit's labels |
221: | Looking | va-g9-look (unit 2, days 13 to 44) | va-g10-look (unit 7) | va-g11-look (unit 12) | va-g12-criticism (unit 17) | How works shape understanding, then how well images sway an audience, then patterns across a type or era, then an extended critical essay |
222: | Judging | va-g9-judge (unit 4, days 81 to 120) | va-g10-judge (unit 9) | va-g11-judge (unit 14) | va-g12-criticism (unit 17) | Standards set, then others' standards tested, then competing readings and several standards, then a defended essay |
223: 
224: Band days: Level 1 is days 1 to 160, Level 2 days 161 to 320, Level 3 days 321 to 480, Level 4 days 481 to 640.
225: 
226: ### Where the threads end
227: 
228: This is the last visual arts course. The four Level 4 rows (va-g12-studio, va-g12-purpose, va-g12-exhibit,
229: va-g12-criticism) hand on nothing: their `hands_on` cells are empty, and the threads end in the Level 4 portfolio,
230: the project, the exhibit and the essay. For a student who stops after Level 3, the threads end in unit 15's show and
231: its year-end check; for a student who stops after Level 1, in the Proficient level, which is a complete course.
